FerrionOS change to userutils (MIT licence, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88:
- when root runs su to a non-root user, apply that user's /etc/login_schemes.toml namespace via userutils::apply_login_schemes and close the prior namespace handle before spawning the shell, keeping root's namespace when targeting root;
- after the sudo daemon accepts the root password in su for a non-root caller, hand over the caller's process handle to obtain root credentials, enter the root namespace only when targeting root, and narrow the caller's current namespace via userutils::apply_login_schemes for any non-root target, closing the prior namespace handle and exiting with an error if any step fails.

